<% faqs << { question: "What is the difference between carving and skidding on a snowboard?", answer: "A skidded turn slides sideways for part of the turn to scrub speed. A carved turn rides on the edge through the whole arc, leaving a thin track in the snow." } %>
<% faqs << { question: "Why does my snowboard skid instead of carve?", answer: "Usually because you're twisting the board with your shoulders instead of tilting it on edge, standing too tall, or leaning back. Get lower and roll your ankles and knees to set the edge." } %>
